        "original_id": "306466c1-97ec-548f-bd56-87ba018d5177",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Fredric Warburg, George Orwell, Thomas Mann, Franz Kafka\n- Works: Animal Farm, Nineteen Eighty-Four\n- Roles: British publisher, English author\n- Topics: publishing, dystopian novel\n\nFacts:\n- Fredric John Warburg was a British publisher who lived from 27 November 1898 to 25 May 1981.\n- Fredric Warburg had a publishing career spanning much of the 20th century and ending in 1971.\n- Fredric Warburg is best known for his association with the author George Orwell.\n- In 1945, Fredric Warburg published George Orwell's Animal Farm.\n- In 1949, Nineteen Eighty-Four, often published as 1984, was published as a dystopian novel by the English author George Orwell.\n- In 1949, Fredric Warburg published George Orwell's Nineteen Eighty-Four.\n- Fredric Warburg also published works by Thomas Mann and Franz Kafka.",
